<title>USA: Most IMM currencies hold gains, yen remains lower.</title>
<headline>Most IMM currencies hold gains, yen remains lower.</headline>
<text>
<p>June 19 - Most IMM currency futures held gains. Sept yen remained lower after President Clinton said he was concerned by the rise in Japan's trade surplus. He said the dollar was strong because the U.S. economy is strong. Sept marks rose through Wed's high of $0.5837. ((DerivativesDesk(312)408-8750))</p>
